    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0548" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1700: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-01T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1925—noon</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>77. Embassy’s 123, November 28, 8 p.m. I am greatly pleased to have your
                    information. In order that you may have background in <pb facs="0549" n="423"
                        xml:id="pg423"/> any future conversations, I wish to restate my position and
                    explain attitude I took in my No. 69, October 31, 2 p.m.<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d257-f1"/></p>
                <p>Nothing would be more gratifying to me than to have a diplomatic settlement of
                    Tacna-Arica question, and there has never been time when I would have hesitated
                    to advise both parties to make settlement of that sort. How to approach them is
                    the difficult question. I am not aware how I could do it without being asked by
                    both parties, as I indicated in my telegram No. 69, and without running great
                    risk of criticism. As soon as both parties ask my good offices, I am willing to
                    advise settlement and to lend my aid in every way.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
